<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>Texas QR and pay-by-phone parking — final map</name>
    <description>Public competitor inventory as of November 15, 2026, America/Chicago. Park&amp;Pay rows are excluded. Revenue figures are estimates except where noted. Coordinates are WGS84 decimal degrees.</description>
    <Folder><name>Top-earning single lots</name>
      <description>Occupancy-adjusted annual revenue estimates for lots with published (or clearly sourced) stall counts and rates. Official venue / kiosk facilities are included and labeled.</description>
      <Placemark>
        <name>#1 Avenida North Garage (Discovery Green / GRB campus)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Avenida North Garage (Discovery Green / GRB campus)</b><br/>
Operator: Houston First (Avenida Houston) / ParkMobile / ParkWhiz<br/>
Address: 1002 Avenida de Las Americas, Houston, TX 77010<br/>
City: Houston<br/>
Spaces: 1848<br/>
Rates: Official posted: $15 (0-1 hr), $25 (1-2 hr), $34 (2-4 hr), $45 daily maximum. Billing cycle typically resets ~2 a.m.<br/>
Pay method: Ticket-on-entry + kiosk; ParkMobile / ParkWhiz reservations<br/>
Confidence: Confirmed pay-by-phone capable (kiosk + reservation)<br/>
Est. annual revenue (low / base / high): $3,353,455 / $5,395,864 / $7,855,981 — ESTIMATE<br/>
Est. weekday / weekend (base): $3,781,452 / $1,614,413<br/>
Coordinates: 29.7531092, -95.3586352 (decimal degrees, WGS84)<br/>
Method: spaces x days x occupancy x turnover x blended rate. Blended rate is an estimate below the $45 daily max to allow for short stays (weekday $28, weekend $32). Occupancy is an estimate: TTI PRC 17-88-F (Jan 2018) found Houston public-garage weekday mean occupancy ~66% (range 52.9-79.9%), but that figure covers all public garages including commuter use and is not applied raw to a convention garage. ParkHouston May 4, 2023 council slides (6 p.m.-midnight curbside, Downtown &amp; East Downtown) show mixed weekday evenings (many blocks under 50%, some 50-79%, a few cores over 80%) and busier but not uniformly full weekend evenings. Convention demand is peaky, so weekday occupancy used here is 28% (scenario) rather than 66%.<br/>
Pay-by-phone capable but not a typical QR walk-up lot. Avenida Central (663 spaces) was listed as temporarily closed, reopen Fall 2026, and is omitted from revenue totals.<br/>
Source: https://www.avenidahouston.com/ and George R. Brown Convention Center parking pages]]></description>
        <Point><coordinates>-95.3586352,29.7531092,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>#2 Tundra Garage (Toyota Center)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Tundra Garage (Toyota Center)</b><br/>
Operator: Toyota Center / ParkMobile (reservations); event operator<br/>
Address: 1510 Polk Street, Houston, TX 77002<br/>
City: Houston<br/>
Spaces: 2478<br/>
Rates: Event-variable; official public pages do not publish a single year-round card. Dollar estimates below use a labeled assumed event rate and should be read as a wide range, not a measured figure.<br/>
Pay method: Event parking; ParkMobile reservations; rates variable<br/>
Confidence: Confirmed pay-by-phone capable (event / reservation)<br/>
Est. annual revenue (low / base / high): $2,173,206 / $4,946,088 / $9,850,050 — ESTIMATE<br/>
Est. weekday / weekend (base): $2,525,259 / $2,420,829<br/>
Coordinates: 29.7507473, -95.3622315 (decimal degrees, WGS84)<br/>
Method: EVENT-RATE ESTIMATE (wide uncertainty). Event days 80, occupancy 55%, assumed event rate $35 (not a published year-round card). Non-event days 285 at 8% occupancy and assumed $20. Weekday/weekend split of event revenue is an estimate (45/55). Do not treat this as a measured figure.<br/>
Treated like official venue parking, not a typical QR walk-up lot. Included in Houston city sensitivity, not used as the QR walk-up #1 lot.<br/>
Source: Official Toyota Center / GRB parking pages]]></description>
        <Point><coordinates>-95.3622315,29.7507473,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>#3 GRB South Garage</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>GRB South Garage</b><br/>
Operator: Houston First (Avenida Houston) / ParkMobile / ParkWhiz<br/>
Address: 1001 Avenida de Las Americas, Houston, TX 77010<br/>
City: Houston<br/>
Spaces: 891<br/>
Rates: Same official card as Avenida North: $15 / $25 / $34 / $45 daily maximum.<br/>
Pay method: Ticket-on-entry + kiosk; ParkMobile / ParkWhiz reservations<br/>
Confidence: Confirmed pay-by-phone capable (kiosk + reservation)<br/>
Est. annual revenue (low / base / high): $1,332,544 / $2,312,829 / $3,275,323 — ESTIMATE<br/>
Est. weekday / weekend (base): $1,627,857 / $684,972<br/>
Coordinates: 29.7517932, -95.3581139 (decimal degrees, WGS84)<br/>
Method: Same rate card as Avenida North. Occupancy set slightly lower than Avenida North (weekday 25%, weekend 22% in this scenario) because this garage is a secondary campus facility. Same TTI 2018 and ParkHouston 2023 caveats apply. Blended rates weekday $28, weekend $32 (estimates below the $45 max).<br/>
Pay-by-phone capable, not typical QR walk-up. Has been recommended as overflow for Toyota Center events while Avenida Central is closed.<br/>
Source: https://www.avenidahouston.com/ and GRB parking pages]]></description>
        <Point><coordinates>-95.3581139,29.7517932,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>#4 Houston Street Garage</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Houston Street Garage</b><br/>
Operator: City of San Antonio / SAPark<br/>
Address: 240 E Houston Street, San Antonio, TX 78205<br/>
City: San Antonio<br/>
Spaces: 900<br/>
Rates: Official example card: $3/hour with a $10 daily cap (Houston Street Garage). Meters are free after 6 p.m. and all day Sunday; some city garage promotions (free after 5 p.m. Tuesdays) also apply. Event rates may be higher.<br/>
Pay method: City garage / SAPark (pay-by-phone / app program)<br/>
Confidence: Confirmed pay-by-app / city garage<br/>
Est. annual revenue (low / base / high): $962,550 / $1,273,266 / $1,577,196 — ESTIMATE<br/>
Est. weekday / weekend (base): $1,057,050 / $216,216<br/>
Coordinates: 29.4263849, -98.4906512 (decimal degrees, WGS84)<br/>
Method: Weekday uses the published $10 daily cap x 45% occupancy x 1.0 turn x 261 days. Weekend uses $5 (the published St. Mary's evenings/weekends visitor rate, also applied here as a conservative weekend visitor rate) x 42% x weekend turnover. High weekend occupancy is capped at 53%, the reported Fiesta 2025 Saturday night downtown-wide peak. Sunday meter-free policy may further reduce weekend paid demand; that is one reason the weekend rate is not set at the weekday cap.<br/>
City-owned. Downtown-wide Fiesta 2025 Saturday night peak occupancy was only 53% (Centro study as reported March 2026 by Axios and CultureMap).<br/>
Source: City of San Antonio parking / ConnectSA; Axios 2026-03-23; CultureMap]]></description>
        <Point><coordinates>-98.4906512,29.4263849,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>#5 Lot 2 / Lot 3</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>Lot 2 / Lot 3</b><br/>
Operator: PMC Pay<br/>
Address: 140 E Exchange Ave, Fort Worth, TX 76164<br/>
City: Fort Worth<br/>
Spaces: 360<br/>
Rates: Official posted rates as of page fetch 2026-11-15: Mon–Wed $12.50, Thu $17.50, Fri–Sun $22.50, overnight $32.50, each plus sales tax and service fee. Premium lots and special events may be higher. Credit card only, no cash. Source: https://fortworthstockyards.com/parking/<br/>
Pay method: Scan QR / text-to-pay<br/>
Confidence: Confirmed QR<br/>
Est. annual revenue (low / base / high): $754,848 / $1,125,058 / $1,564,308 — ESTIMATE<br/>
Est. weekday / weekend (base): $355,680 / $769,379<br/>
Coordinates: 32.7888193, -97.3487563 (decimal degrees, WGS84)<br/>
Method: Official Stockyards rate card (page fetch 2026-11-15, America/Chicago): Mon-Wed $12.50 x 156d, Thu $17.50 x 52d, Fri-Sun $22.50 x 157d. Occupancy (base): Mon-Wed 32%, Thu 40%, Fri-Sun 55% with Fri-Sun turnover 1.10. Tax and service fee excluded. Occupancy is an estimate informed by tourist-weekend peaking; no official Stockyards occupancy study was located.<br/>
Official Stockyards lots; PMC operates; Mon–Wed $12.50 · Thu $17.50 · Fri–Sun $22.50 · overnight $32.50 (+tax/fee); no cash<br/>
Source: https://fortworthstockyards.com/parking/ + parkingmgt.com]]></description>
        <Point><coordinates>-97.3487563,32.7888193,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>#6 St. Mary's Garage</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<b>St. Mary's Garage</b><br/>
Operator: City of San Antonio / SAPark<br/>
Address: 205 E Travis Street, San Antonio, TX 78205<br/>
City: San Antonio<br/>
Spaces: 704<br/>
Rates: Official: $5 evenings and weekends; $15 event. Free parking is sometimes offered on Majestic Theatre nights except major Broadway / sold-out performances. Weekday daytime cap is treated as $10 in the estimate where a visitor uses the garage by day (same city-garage daily-cap example as Houston Street).<br/>
Pay method: City garage / SAPark (pay-by-phone / app program)<br/>
Confidence: Confirmed pay-by-app / city garage<br/>
Est. annual revenue (low / base / high): $752,928 / $995,977 / $1,233,718 — ESTIMATE<br/>
Est. weekday / weekend (base): $826,848 / $169,129<br/>
Coordinates: 29.4276301, -98.4911389 (decimal degrees, WGS84)<br/>
Method: Weekday $10 cap x 45% occupancy; weekend $5 evenings/weekends rate x 42%. High weekend occupancy capped at the reported 53% Fiesta 2025 Saturday night downtown-wide peak. Promotional free nights and $15 event nights are not modeled day-by-day and are a source of variance.<br/>
City-owned, steps from the River Walk. Fiesta 2025 Saturday night peak occupancy downtown-wide was 53%.<br/>
Source: City of San Antonio parking / ConnectSA; Axios 2026-03-23]]></description>
        <Point><coordinates>-98.4911389,29.4276301,0</coordinates></Point>
      </Placemark>
